          "inputs": [],
          "type": "START"
        },
        {
          "metadata": {
            "description": "End of data pipeline",
            "name": "End"
          },
          "outcomes": {},
          "code": "END",
          "id": "end",
          "inputs": [],
          "type": "END"
        },
        {
          "metadata": {
            "name": "modelType_check"
          },
          "outcomes": {
            "true": "1770904748231",
            "false": "1770904796195"
          },
          "code": "MODELTYPECHECK",
          "convergenceTargetId": "end",
          "id": "1770904700627",
          "inputs": [
            {
              "id": "1770904700629_1",
              "name": "condition",
              "type": "string",
              "value": "{{$context.$nodes.CREATE_WORKFLOW_CONTEXT.$output.result.classificationModel}}"
            }
          ],
          "type": "CONDITION"
        },
        {
          "metadata": {
            "name": "classificationSuccessCriteriaCheck"
          },
          "outcomes": {
            "true": "1770973532816",
            "false": "1770974387456"
          },
          "code": "CLASSIFICATIONSUCCESSCRITERIACHECK",
          "convergenceTargetId": "end",
          "id": "1770904748231",
          "inputs": [
            {
              "id": "1770904748233_1",
              "name": "condition",
              "type": "string",
              "value": "{{$context.$nodes.CREATE_WORKFLOW_CONTEXT.$output.result.hasSuccessCriteria}}"
            }
          ],
          "type": "CONDITION"
        },
        {
          "metadata": {
            "name": "regressionSuccessCriteriaCheck"
          },
          "outcomes": {
            "true": "1770974867401",
            "false": "1770975070435"
          },
          "code": "REGRESSIONSUCCESSCRITERIACHECK",
          "convergenceTargetId": "end",
          "id": "1770904796195",
          "inputs": [
            {
              "id": "1770904796197_1",
              "name": "condition",
              "type": "string",
              "value": "{{$context.$nodes.CREATE_WORKFLOW_CONTEXT.$output.result.hasSuccessCriteria}}"
            }
          ],
          "type": "CONDITION"
        },
        {
          "metadata": {
            "name": "CreateWorkflowContext",
            "returnType": "object",
            "sourceCode": "const modelType = $context.$triggers.REST.$input.modelType;\nconst classificationModel = ( modelType.toLowerCase() == \"classification\" ) ? true : false;\nconst successCriteria = $context.$triggers.REST.$input.successCriteria;\nconst hasSuccessCriteria = ( successCriteria && successCriteria != \"\" ) ? true : false;\nlet workflowContext = { \"classificationModel\" : classificationModel, \"hasSuccessCriteria\" : hasSuccessCriteria };\nreturn workflowContext;"
          },
          "outcomes": {
            "success": "1770904700627"
          },
          "code": "CREATE_WORKFLOW_CONTEXT",
          "id": "1770964516928",
          "inputs": [],
          "outputSpecification": "{\n  \"$schema\": \"http://json-schema.org/draft-04/schema#\",\n  \"type\": \"object\",\n  \"properties\": {\n    \"result\": {\n      \"type\": \"object\"\n    },\n    \"timeout\": {\n      \"type\": \"boolean\"\n    },\n    \"error\": {\n      \"type\": \"string\"\n    }\n  },\n  \"required\": [\n    \"output\",\n    \"timeout\",\n    \"error\"\n  ]\n}",
          "type": "CODE"
        },
        {
          "metadata": {
            "name": "Generate Explanation - Classification w Success Criteria"
          },
          "outcomes": {
            "success": "end"
          },
          "code": "GENERATE_EXPLANATION_CLASSIFICATION_W_SUCCESS_CRITERIA",
          "id": "1770973532816",
          "inputs": [
            {
              "id": "1770973532817_1",
              "name": "prompt",
              "type": "string",
              "value": "##Input\nBased on outcome of a {{$context.$triggers.REST.$input.modelType }}  AI model, we have following prediction for a {{$context.$triggers.REST.$input.object}} . Predicted success probability for the {{$context.$triggers.REST.$input.object}} is {{$context.$triggers.REST.$input.successProbability}} . Success is defined as {{$context.$triggers.REST.$input.successCriteria}} . Factors positively impacting the prediction are {{$context.$triggers.REST.$input.positiveFactors}} Factors negatively impacting the prediction are {{$context.$triggers.REST.$input.negativeFactors}}.\n\n\n##Context\nPositive factors have ideal values for the successful outcome\nNegative factors have values that fall outside the ideal range for successful outcome\nPositive factors and negative factors may contain related object and its attribute, formatted as Object.Attribute\n\n##instructions\nPositive factors <Provide an explanation for each factor and how it impacts the prediction to a sales representative in no more than 250 words>\nNegative factors <Provide an explanation for each factor and how it impacts the prediction to a sales representative in no more than 250 words>\nNext Actions <Provide bullet list of up to 3 key next steps/recommendations to improve the outcome>\nUse Professional tone\nDo not assume details that are not provided\n\n##Output\nOutput an RFC8259-compliant JSON object containing explanations for positive_factors, negative_factors, next_actions and model. Do not wrap the response in triple backticks or any code block.\nThe returned output can have keys positive_factors, negative_factors, next_actions and model. The values for positive_factors, negative_factors and next_actions should be an array, an array of type strings. The positive_factors and negative_factors need to only exist if there are any explanations provided, i.e. if there are no positive factors provided as input you don't need to output an key value positive_factors for the explanations and the similar for negative_factors. The model should have value \"classification with success criteria\", this lets us identify the llm node that returned the result ( for debugging )."
            }
          ],
          "outputSpecification": "{\n  \"positive_factors\": [\n    \"The sales opportunity is in the High Tech industry, which is a favorable sector for your products and services. This industry often has a higher propensity to adopt innovative solutions, and your Green Server 56042 and associated AMC (Asset Management Contract) offerings are well-aligned with their needs.\",\n    \"The account's segment is Mid-size, indicating a business that is large enough to have significant IT requirements but not so large that it is overly risk-averse. This segment often has a good balance between budget and decision-making agility, making it an attractive target for your sales efforts.\",\n    \"The account has a healthy number of Activities (14), suggesting that there has been consistent engagement and interest from the client's side. This level of activity often indicates a higher chance of conversion, as it shows a sustained level of interest and interaction with your sales team.\",\n    \"The account's number of employees falls within the range of 0 to 20,000, which is a positive indicator. This range suggests that the account is a well-established business with a substantial workforce, providing a larger potential market for your products and services.\"\n  ],\n  \"negative_factors\": [\n    \"The presence of a competitor, Global Tech Giant, in this sales opportunity is a cause for concern. This competitor likely has significant market share and resources, which could make it challenging to displace them as the preferred vendor.\",\n    \"The key decision-maker for this account is not identified, which is a potential roadblock. Having a clear understanding of who holds the decision-making power is crucial for tailoring your sales approach and building relationships with the right individuals.\",\n    \"The account's organization name, Sun Microsystems US, may indicate that this is a well-established and mature business. Mature businesses often have more stringent procurement processes and may be less open to new vendors, especially if they have a long-standing relationship with a competitor.\"\n  ],\n  \"next_actions\": [\n    \"Focus on differentiating your products and services from those of Global Tech Giant. Highlight the unique value proposition of Green Server 56042 and its associated AMC, emphasizing any features or benefits that set it apart from the competition.\",\n    \"Identify and engage with the key decision-makers within Sun Microsystems US. Understand their pain points and how your solutions can address them. Building relationships with these individuals will be crucial to overcoming any existing vendor preferences.\",\n    \"Leverage the positive factors, such as the account's industry and segment, to tailor your sales approach. Emphasize how your solutions are well-suited to the High Tech industry and can help mid-size businesses like Sun Microsystems US achieve their goals.\"\n  ],\n  \"model\" : \"classification with success criteria\"\n}",
          "type": "LLM"
        },
        {
          "metadata": {
            "name": "Generate Explanations - Classification wo Success Criteria"
          },
          "outcomes": {
            "success": "end"
          },
          "code": "GENERATE_EXPLANATIONS_CLASSIFICATION_WO_SUCCESS_CRITERIA",
          "id": "1770974387456",
          "inputs": [
            {
              "id": "1770974387457_1",
              "name": "prompt",
              "type": "string",
              "value": "##Input\nBased on outcome of a {{$context.$triggers.REST.$input.modelType }} AI model, we have following prediction for a {{$context.$triggers.REST.$input.object}}. Predicted value for {{$context.$triggers.REST.$input.object}} is {{$context.$triggers.REST.$input.predictedValue}} with a probability of {{$context.$triggers.REST.$input.predictionProbability}}. Factors impacting the prediction are {{$context.$triggers.REST.$input.factorsList}}\n\n##Context\nDo not assume if given number factor value is high or low compared to ideal value\n\n##instructions\nFactors impacting the prediction <Provide an explanation for each factor and how it may impact the prediction to a sales representative in no more than 500 words>\nNext Actions <Provide bullet list of up to 3 key next steps/recommendations to improve the outcome>\nUse Professional tone\nDo not assume details that are not provided\n\n## Output Format\nOutput an RFC8259-compliant JSON object containing explanations for factors, next actions and model details. Do not wrap the response in triple backticks or any code block.\nThe returned output should have keys explanations, next_actions and model. The values for explanations, and next_actions should be an array of strings. The model should have value \"classification without success criteria\", this lets us identify the llm node that returned the result ( for debugging )."
            }
          ],
          "outputSpecification": "{\n  \"explanations\": [\n   \"The country of the sales lead, being the USA, may impact the prediction as it could indicate a larger market and potentially a more competitive environment. This could influence the time taken to convert the lead, as there may be a higher number of similar businesses and a more saturated market.\",\n   \"The industry, High Tech, is a relevant factor as it often involves innovative and rapidly changing technologies. This industry may have a higher barrier to entry and a longer sales cycle, especially for new or complex products. The prediction of 188 days could be influenced by the need for thorough research and decision-making processes within the High Tech sector.\",\n   \"The rank of 'Hot' suggests that this lead is considered a priority and has a higher potential for conversion. A higher rank often indicates a more qualified lead with a greater likelihood of becoming a customer. This factor may positively impact the prediction, as it implies a stronger interest and a faster potential conversion time.\",\n    \"The number of activities, 5, could refer to various interactions or touchpoints with the sales lead. A higher number of activities might indicate a more engaged lead and a stronger relationship. This factor can be positive, as it shows a level of interest and involvement, which could lead to a quicker conversion. However, the prediction still estimates a longer conversion time, so further analysis is needed to understand any potential barriers.\",\n    \"The absence of a key decision-maker within the lead's organization may impact the prediction. Identifying and engaging with the right decision-makers is crucial for a successful sales process. Without a clear decision-maker, the conversion time could be extended, as it might require more time to identify and build a relationship with the appropriate person.\",\n    \"The account's number of employees, ranging from 0 to 20,000, provides an indication of the company's size. Smaller companies may have a faster decision-making process and a more agile approach. However, the prediction suggests a longer conversion time, which could be influenced by other factors such as the complexity of the sale or the need for multiple approvals within the organization.\"\n  ],\n  \"next_steps\": [\n    \"Conduct a thorough analysis of the competition within the USA, especially in the High Tech industry, to understand the unique value proposition and differentiate the offering.\",\n    \"Identify and engage with the key decision-makers within the organization. Building a strong relationship and understanding their decision-making process can help expedite the conversion.\",\n    \"Given the predicted conversion time, consider implementing a tailored nurturing campaign to keep the lead engaged and interested. This could involve a series of targeted communications and interactions to maintain momentum and guide the lead through the sales funnel.\"\n  ],\n  \"model\" : \"classification without success criteria\"\n}",
          "type": "LLM"
        },
        {
          "metadata": {
            "name": "Generate Explanations - Regression w Success Criteria"
          },
          "outcomes": {
            "success": "end"
          },
          "code": "GENERATE_EXPLANATIONS_REGRESSION_W_SUCCESS_CRITERIA",
          "id": "1770974867401",
          "inputs": [
            {
              "id": "1770974867402_1",
              "name": "prompt",
              "type": "string",
              "value": "##Input\nBased on outcome of a {{$context.$triggers.REST.$input.modelType}} AI model, we have following prediction for a {{$context.$triggers.REST.$input.object}} . Predicted {{$context.$triggers.REST.$input.target}} for the {{$context.$triggers.REST.$input.object}}  is {{$context.$triggers.REST.$input.predictedValue}} . {{$context.$triggers.REST.$input.target}} is considered as {{$context.$triggers.REST.$input.successCriteria}} . Factors positively impacting the prediction are {{$context.$triggers.REST.$input.positiveFactors}} . Factors negatively impacting the prediction are {{$context.$triggers.REST.$input.negativeFactors}} .\n\n##Context\nPositive factors have ideal values for the successful outcome\nNegative factors have values that fall outside the ideal range for successful outcome\nPositive factors and negative factors may contain related object and its attribute, formatted as Object.Attribute\n\n##instructions\nPositive factors <Provide an explanation for each factor and how it impacts the prediction to a sales representative in no more than 250 words>\nNegative factors <Provide an explanation for each factor and how it impacts the prediction to a sales representative in no more than 250 words>\nNext Actions <Provide bullet list of up to 3 key next steps/recommendations to improve the outcome>\nUse Professional tone\nDo not assume details that are not provided\n\n## Output Format\nOutput an RFC8259-compliant JSON object containing explanations for positive_factors, negative_factors, next_actions and model. Do not wrap the response in triple backticks or any code block.\nThe returned output should have keys positive_factors, negative_factors, next_actions and model. The values for positive_factors, negative_factors and next_actions should be an array, an array of type strings. The positive_factors and negative_factors need to only exist if there are any explanations provided, i.e. if there are no positive factors provided as input you don't need to output an key value positive_factors for the explanations and the similar for negative_factors. The model should have value \"regression with success criteria\", this lets us identify the llm node that returned the result ( for debugging )."
            }
          ],
          "outputSpecification": "{\n  \"positive_factors\": [\n    \"The sales opportunity is in the High Tech industry, which is a favorable sector for your products and services. This industry often has a higher propensity to adopt innovative solutions, and your Green Server 56042 and associated AMC (Asset Management Contract) offerings are well-aligned with their needs.\",\n    \"The account's segment is Mid-size, indicating a business that is large enough to have significant IT requirements but not so large that it is overly risk-averse. This segment often has a good balance between budget and decision-making agility, making it an attractive target for your sales efforts.\",\n    \"The account has a healthy number of Activities (14), suggesting that there has been consistent engagement and interest from the client's side. This level of activity often indicates a higher chance of conversion, as it shows a sustained level of interest and interaction with your sales team.\",\n    \"The account's number of employees falls within the range of 0 to 20,000, which is a positive indicator. This range suggests that the account is a well-established business with a substantial workforce, providing a larger potential market for your products and services.\"\n  ],\n  \"negative_factors\": [\n    \"The presence of a competitor, Global Tech Giant, in this sales opportunity is a cause for concern. This competitor likely has significant market share and resources, which could make it challenging to displace them as the preferred vendor.\",\n    \"The key decision-maker for this account is not identified, which is a potential roadblock. Having a clear understanding of who holds the decision-making power is crucial for tailoring your sales approach and building relationships with the right individuals.\",\n    \"The account's organization name, Sun Microsystems US, may indicate that this is a well-established and mature business. Mature businesses often have more stringent procurement processes and may be less open to new vendors, especially if they have a long-standing relationship with a competitor.\"\n  ],\n  \"next_actions\": [\n    \"Focus on differentiating your products and services from those of Global Tech Giant. Highlight the unique value proposition of Green Server 56042 and its associated AMC, emphasizing any features or benefits that set it apart from the competition.\",\n    \"Identify and engage with the key decision-makers within Sun Microsystems US. Understand their pain points and how your solutions can address them. Building relationships with these individuals will be crucial to overcoming any existing vendor preferences.\",\n    \"Leverage the positive factors, such as the account's industry and segment, to tailor your sales approach. Emphasize how your solutions are well-suited to the High Tech industry and can help mid-size businesses like Sun Microsystems US achieve their goals.\"\n  ],\n  \"model\" : \"regression with success criteria\"\n}",
          "type": "LLM"
        },
        {
          "metadata": {
            "name": "Generate Explanations - Regression wo Success Criteria"
          },
          "outcomes": {
            "success": "end"
          },
          "code": "GENERATE_EXPLANATIONS_REGRESSION_WO_SUCCESS_CRITERIA",
          "id": "1770975070435",
          "inputs": [
            {
              "id": "1770975070436_1",
              "name": "prompt",
              "type": "string",
              "value": "##Input\nBased on outcome of a {{$context.$triggers.REST.$input.modelType}} AI model, we have following prediction for a {{$context.$triggers.REST.$input.object}} . Predicted {{$context.$triggers.REST.$input.target}} for the {{$context.$triggers.REST.$input.object}} is {{$context.$triggers.REST.$input.predictedValue}} . Factors impacting the prediction are {{$context.$triggers.REST.$input.factorsList}} .\n\n##Context\nDo not assume if a number factor value is higher of lower than ideal\n\n##instructions\nExplanation <Provide an explanation for each factor and how it impacts the prediction to a sales representative in no more than 500 words>\nNext Actions <Provide bullet list of up to 3 key next steps/recommendations to improve the outcome>\nFactors may contain related object and its attribute, formatted as Object.Attribute\nUse Professional tone\nDo not assume details that are not provided\n\n## Output Format\nOutput an RFC8259-compliant JSON object containing explanations for factors, next actions and model details. Do not wrap the response in triple backticks or any code block.\nThe returned output should have keys explanations, next_actions and model. The values for explanations, and next_actions should be an array of strings. The model should have value \"regression without success criteria\", this lets us identify the llm node that returned the result ( for debugging )."
            }
          ],
          "outputSpecification": "{\n  \"explanations\": [\n   \"The country of the sales lead, being the USA, may impact the prediction as it could indicate a larger market and potentially a more competitive environment. This could influence the time taken to convert the lead, as there may be a higher number of similar businesses and a more saturated market.\",\n   \"The industry, High Tech, is a relevant factor as it often involves innovative and rapidly changing technologies. This industry may have a higher barrier to entry and a longer sales cycle, especially for new or complex products. The prediction of 188 days could be influenced by the need for thorough research and decision-making processes within the High Tech sector.\",\n   \"The rank of 'Hot' suggests that this lead is considered a priority and has a higher potential for conversion. A higher rank often indicates a more qualified lead with a greater likelihood of becoming a customer. This factor may positively impact the prediction, as it implies a stronger interest and a faster potential conversion time.\",\n    \"The number of activities, 5, could refer to various interactions or touchpoints with the sales lead. A higher number of activities might indicate a more engaged lead and a stronger relationship. This factor can be positive, as it shows a level of interest and involvement, which could lead to a quicker conversion. However, the prediction still estimates a longer conversion time, so further analysis is needed to understand any potential barriers.\",\n    \"The absence of a key decision-maker within the lead's organization may impact the prediction. Identifying and engaging with the right decision-makers is crucial for a successful sales process. Without a clear decision-maker, the conversion time could be extended, as it might require more time to identify and build a relationship with the appropriate person.\",\n    \"The account's number of employees, ranging from 0 to 20,000, provides an indication of the company's size. Smaller companies may have a faster decision-making process and a more agile approach. However, the prediction suggests a longer conversion time, which could be influenced by other factors such as the complexity of the sale or the need for multiple approvals within the organization.\"\n  ],\n  \"next_steps\": [\n    \"Conduct a thorough analysis of the competition within the USA, especially in the High Tech industry, to understand the unique value proposition and differentiate the offering.\",\n    \"Identify and engage with the key decision-makers within the organization. Building a strong relationship and understanding their decision-making process can help expedite the conversion.\",\n    \"Given the predicted conversion time, consider implementing a tailored nurturing campaign to keep the lead engaged and interested. This could involve a series of targeted communications and interactions to maintain momentum and guide the lead through the sales funnel.\"\n  ],\n  \"model\" : \"regression without success criteria\"\n}",
          "type": "LLM"
        }
      ],
